From 2cc79f39c85f2989f9ef341f07558a07626f2a1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irregularthanis <343663069+irregularthanis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:10:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 205/205] Aurora: efficient soft effects, an opt-in half-size
 buffer for haze and smoke

Runs of eight or more large see-through quads drawn after the scene (blended
source alpha over inverse source alpha, no depth test or write, one TEV
stage, one or two triangles per draw) are drawn into a buffer of half the
EFB's size and blended over the EFB once, in the same place in the draw
order. The buffer accumulates premultiplied colour and coverage (alpha
factors One, OneMinusSrcAlpha, through a softTarget pipeline variant), so
the composite (One, OneMinusSrcAlpha) gives the colour each quad blended in
turn would; only the resolution differs. Viewports and scissors are halved in
the buffer, a run whose variants are still compiling keeps the EFB, and the
real frame and the in-between replay take the same path.

At render scale 3 on a Steam Deck the Lava Room's heat haze (81 quads) was
about 15 of the frame's 23 ms of GPU time, and the Shipwreck's veil about
62% of its frame. aurora_set_efficient_effects turns it on (off by default),
for EFBs 1280 or more pixels wide. GXCore pipeline config v14.

soft_effects_test covers the rule against the draw states logged in those
rooms, the runs, and the blend identity over 2,000 random stacks.
